---
import SourceNote from './SourceNote.astro';
import { number, type CityView } from '../../lib/city-v2';
interface Props { city: CityView; }
const { city } = Astro.props;
const rows = city.industries;
---
{rows.length > 0 && <section class="section" id="trade-density" aria-labelledby="trade-title">
  <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Employer establishments · postal-area context</p><h2 id="trade-title">ZIP-area density, not city competition</h2><p>Counts cover employer establishments in the source’s postal ZIP set. The resident denominator uses corresponding statistical ZIP areas. Neither boundary is the city limit.</p></div>
  <div class="scope-note"><strong>Read the boundary before the number.</strong> Density is a descriptive ratio, not evidence of unmet demand, available capacity or profitability. Nonemployer businesses are outside this count.</div>
  <div class="table-scroll" role="region" aria-label="ZIP-area trade density" tabindex="0">
    <table class="trade-table">
      <caption>ZIP-area employer density per ten thousand residents</caption>
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Industry / classification</th><th scope="col">Employer establishments</th><th scope="col">ZIP-area density</th><th scope="col">National reference</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>{rows.map(r => <tr data-fact-path={`industries.${r.index}`}>
        <th scope="row">{r.label}<span class="classification" data-value-path={`industries.${r.index}.naicsCode`} data-format="text">{r.naicsCode}</span>
          <details class="row-source"><summary>Source & denominator</summary>
            <p data-evidence-path={`industries.${r.index}.provenance.evidenceQuote`}>{r.provenance.evidenceQuote}</p>
            <p class="small">Numerator: employer establishments in the linked business-patterns dataset. Denominator: statistical ZIP-area population identified in the evidence quote, not city population.</p>
            {city.stats[0] && <p class="small"><a href={city.stats[0].source.url}>Population denominator dataset</a></p>}
            <SourceNote source={r.sourceNote} />
          </details>
        </th>
        <td data-value-path={`industries.${r.index}.establishments`} data-format="number">{number(r.establishments)}</td>
        <td data-value-path={`industries.${r.index}.per10kResidents`} data-format="number">{number(r.per10kResidents)}</td>
        <td data-value-path={`industries.${r.index}.usAvgPer10k`} data-format="number">{number(r.usAvgPer10k)}</td>
      </tr>)}</tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  {rows[0] && <SourceNote source={rows[0].sourceNote} />}
</section>}
